From 9ba742257aadcbf628c84f2830d9fc84b9009288 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 341/488] soh: name the 14 address-named symbols defined in
 z_en_niw_lady.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 14 are defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Niw_Lady/z_en_niw_lady.c; updating their references touches 2 files in total.

  * D_80ABB3B4 -> sCuccoInfTableBits
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the infTable[25] bit each numbered Cucco owns,
    set while it is inside the pen and cleared while it is out.

  * func_80AB9F24 -> EnNiwLady_WaitForObjects
    deduced, confidence HIGH: waits for both of Anju's object banks, then
    builds the skeleton, collider and shape, picks her starting animation
    and installs the age-appropriate action.

  * func_80ABA21C -> EnNiwLady_SetupCuccoCount
    deduced, confidence HIGH: arms the missing-Cucco line and installs the
    counting action.

  * func_80ABA244 -> EnNiwLady_CountCuccos
    deduced, confidence HIGH: walks the prop actor list each frame, counting
    the Cuccos inside the pen and recording each one's infTable bit, and
    picks Anju's line from the total.

  * func_80ABA654 -> EnNiwLady_FinishCuccoTalk
    deduced, confidence HIGH: once the counting line is advanced it hands
    over the bottle the first time all the Cuccos are penned, or a purple
    rupee afterwards, and otherwise returns to counting.

  * func_80ABA778 -> EnNiwLady_SetupAdultTalk
    deduced, confidence HIGH: picks the adult-era line from how far the
    Pocket Egg and Cojiro trade has progressed and installs the adult talk
    action.

  * func_80ABA878 -> EnNiwLady_AdultTalk
    deduced, confidence HIGH: offers talk in the adult era and routes the
    accepted conversation into whichever trade prompt the current line calls
    for.

  * func_80ABA9B8 -> EnNiwLady_OfferPocketEgg
    deduced, confidence HIGH: resolves the first trade prompt: yes hands
    over GI_POCKET_EGG, no shows the refusal line.

  * func_80ABAB08 -> EnNiwLady_OfferCojiro
    deduced, confidence HIGH: resolves the second trade prompt: yes hands
    over GI_COJIRO, no shows the refusal line and records it.

  * func_80ABAA9C -> EnNiwLady_DeclineTrade
    deduced, confidence HIGH: waits out the refusal line and returns to the
    adult talk setup.

  * func_80ABAC00 -> EnNiwLady_GiveItem
    deduced, confidence HIGH: re-offers the current trade item until the
    player takes it.

  * func_80ABAC84 -> EnNiwLady_FinishGiveItem
    deduced, confidence HIGH: waits out the get-item textbox and sets the
    trade or bottle flag for whichever item was just handed over.

  * func_80ABAD38 -> EnNiwLady_SetupIdleTalk
    deduced, confidence HIGH: arms the ordinary greeting and installs the
    idle talk action.

  * func_80ABAD7C -> EnNiwLady_IdleTalk
    deduced, confidence HIGH: offers talk with the ordinary greeting or the
    mask face reaction, and records that the player has spoken to her.

